op {
  graph_op_name: "QuantizeAndDequantizeV3"
  in_arg {
    name: "input_min"
    description: <<END
If `range_given == True`, this specifies the minimum input value that needs to
be represented, otherwise it is determined from the min value of the `input`
tensor.

If `axis` is specified, the shape of the minimum input tensor
must be rank 1.
END
  }
  in_arg {
    name: "input_max"
    description: <<END
If `range_given == True`, this specifies the maximum input value that needs to
be represented, otherwise it is determined from the max value of the `input`
tensor.

If `axis` is specified, the shape of the maximum input tensor
must be rank 1.
END
  }
  summary: "Quantizes then dequantizes a tensor."
  description: <<END
This is almost identical to QuantizeAndDequantizeV2, except that num_bits is a
tensor, so its value can change during training.
END
}
